# What `docker build` (and `fly deploy`) leaves out of the build context, so the
# upload stays small and the image never picks up local state.
#
# The Dockerfile copies only Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, build.rs, src/, examples/,
# packs/, LICENSE and NOTICE. Everything below is something it does not need. Do not add
# examples/ or packs/ here: build.rs compiles them into the binary as the
# shipped read-only spaces, README.md files and data/ folders included.

# Rust build output: gigabytes, and the image builds its own.
target/

# Local spaces and their working state: these belong on the server's volume,
# not baked into an image. Also any .lorefile/ folder (proposals, activity log).
spaces/
**/.lorefile/

# The static docs site (published by Vercel, see vercel.json), the scripts that
# build it and install releases, and the npm launcher package.
docs/
scripts/
npm/

# Version control, CI, editor and agent settings.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.mcp.json
**/.DS_Store

# Tests, design notes and specs: not part of the binary.
tests/
design/
specs/

# Top-level Markdown docs (README.md, DEPLOY.md, ...). This pattern matches the
# top level only, so examples/*/README.md and packs/*/README.md still go in.
*.md

# Deploy config for the hosts themselves. (The Dockerfile stays in: some
# builders read it from the context.)
fly.toml
vercel.json
.vercelignore
